        "id": 1000187
      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-12-23T01:16:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmm.  One advantage of keeping this implementation is that it only requires a stack buffer if flash isn\u0027t directly mapped into memory.  ssl, what do you think?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 173,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 175,
        "endChar": 6
      },
      "revId": "31a58c66b91291ba74290a30516414fb21f1843d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a1d04c89_ce727702",
        "filename": "common/sha256.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 175,
      "author": {
        "id": 1110619
      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-12-23T02:13:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Goal: remove  CONFIG_SHRSPI_ARCH and support both flash \n(directly mapped flash and not directly mapped flash).\nLess ifdef in C code is better.\n\n\nSuggestions:\n\n1.  add int flash_is_memory_mapped(void); for all platforms.\n\n\n2. avoid local stack var becomes too big.\n   move \n     uint8_t shifted_data_buf[SHA256_BLOCK_SIZE]; \n     and uint8_t *shifted_data \n\ninto sha256_ctx:\n     \n\n/* SHA256 context */\nstruct sha256_ctx {\n        uint32_t h[8];\n        uint32_t tot_len;\n        uint32_t len;\n        uint8_t block[2 * SHA256_BLOCK_SIZE];\n        uint8_t buf[SHA256_DIGEST_SIZE];  /* Used to store the final digest. */\n        uint8_t *shifted_data;\n        uint8_t shifted_data_buf[SHA256_BLOCK_SIZE];\n\n};",
      "parentUuid": "019678c9_c11c4695",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 173,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 175,
        "endChar": 6
      },
      "revId": "31a58c66b91291ba74290a30516414fb21f1843d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e17b245e_4b092d4c",
        "filename": "common/sha256.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 175,
      "author": {
        "id": 1121210
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-05-28T03:21:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually, we did support memory mapping for spi flash.\r\nThe mapped address of spi flash is 0x64000000.\r\nWe also can use memcpy for sha256 operation.\r\nFor example,\r\nflash_tristate(0);\r\nmemcpy(\u0026ctx-\u003eblock[ctx-\u003elen], data, rem_len);\r\nflash_tristate(1);\r\n\r\nThe item we like to discuss is when we can disable tri-state of flash if EC share the same flash with BIOS. It\u0027s dangerous to disable tri-state when BIOS didn\u0027t release the control of spi pins.\r\n\r\nAnd if you think it\u0027s a big effort to ask BIOS team support that, we also have the other version which support stand-alone spi flash.(EC didn\u0027t share  spi flash with BIOS) This version minimize the changes of common layer sources. (Only slight change for sysjump. And sha256.c and flash.c are the same with older version.) But we still think shared-spi arch is a better choice for cost.",
      "parentUuid": "a1d04c89_ce727702",
      "revId": "31a58c66b91291ba74290a30516414fb21f1843d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e16404ca_80b79af5",
        "filename": "common/sha256.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 182,
